1 REM FBCS ECMA-0069
2 REM CLAIM A-ECMA-30
3 REM TYPE SELF
100 REM ERASE DELETES ALL FILE ELEMENTS: THE FILE BECOMES EMPTY AND THE POINTER IS AT END OF FILE (L.6913-6920)
110 REM ERASE REST DELETES THE ELEMENTS AT OR BEYOND THE POINTER, KEEPS THE PRECEDING ONES, POINTER TO END (L.6922-6925)
120 REM ASK DATUM IS WELL-DEFINED FOR STREAM INTERNAL FILES; ASK RECORD GIVES 0 FOR A NON-RELATIVE FILE (L.6964-6973, L.7013-7015)
125 REM EACH VALUE IS WRITTEN BY ITS OWN WRITE (ONE VALUE PER FILE ELEMENT, L.6743-6752)
130 OPEN #3: NAME "ECMA0069A.DAT", ACCESS OUTIN, ORGANIZATION STREAM, RECTYPE INTERNAL
140 WRITE #3: 1, "A"
150 ERASE #3
160 ASK #3: POINTER P1$, DATUM D1$, RECORD R1
170 CLOSE #3
180 OPEN #4: NAME "ECMA0069B.DAT", ACCESS OUTIN, ORGANIZATION STREAM, RECTYPE INTERNAL
190 WRITE #4: 1
195 WRITE #4: 2
197 WRITE #4: 3
200 SET #4: POINTER BEGIN
210 READ #4: X
220 ERASE REST #4
230 ASK #4: POINTER P2$, DATUM D2$
240 SET #4: POINTER BEGIN
250 READ #4: Y
260 ASK #4: POINTER P3$, DATUM D3$
270 CLOSE #4
272 REM A MULTI-VALUE WRITE IS STILL A SEQUENCE OF INDIVIDUAL VALUES: POINTER AND ERASE REST WORK PER VALUE (L.6743-6752)
273 OPEN #5: NAME "ECMA0069C.DAT", ACCESS OUTIN, ORGANIZATION STREAM, RECTYPE INTERNAL
274 WRITE #5: 1, 2, 3
275 SET #5: POINTER BEGIN
276 READ #5: X5
277 ASK #5: POINTER P4$
278 ERASE REST #5
279 SET #5: POINTER BEGIN
281 READ #5: Y5
282 ASK #5: POINTER P5$, DATUM D5$
283 CLOSE #5
300 IF P1$ = "END" AND D1$ = "NONE" AND R1 = 0 AND X = 1 AND P2$ = "END" AND D2$ = "NONE" &
&AND Y = 1 AND P3$ = "END" AND D3$ = "NONE" AND P4$ = "MIDDLE" AND X5 = 1 AND Y5 = 1 &
&AND P5$ = "END" AND D5$ = "NONE" THEN
310    PRINT "*** TEST PASSED ***"
320 ELSE
330    PRINT "*** TEST FAILED: ["; P1$; "] ["; D1$; "]"; R1; X; "["; P2$; "] ["; D2$; "]"; Y; "["; P3$; "] ["; D3$; "]"; &
&P4$; X5; Y5; P5$; D5$
340 END IF
350 END
